# Subcategory i18n: scripts and parallel work

When refactoring subcategory pages to load only their own translations (like article pages):

1. **Prefer scripts** so one agent does not load all category JSONs and consume the whole context:
   - `node scripts/extract-subcategory-jsons.mjs` — create subcategory-*.json from category-*.json
   - `node scripts/update-subcategory-pages.mjs` — switch getStaticProps and @pages to getSubcategoryNamespace (add new pairs to PAIRS in script if needed)
   - `node scripts/trim-category-jsons.mjs` — trim category JSONs to title, description, and subcategories.{id}.{ title, shortDesc } only

2. **After trim**, category JSONs must not contain full subcategory content (sections, stats, etc.); that lives only in subcategory-{category}-{sub}.json.

3. For **parallel agents**: one agent per (categoryId, subcategoryId). Each agent handles one pair (create 4 JSONs + update 2 page files + @pages ns). Follow `.cursor/skills/subcategory-i18n-split/SKILL.md`. Run trim script once after all subcategory work is done.
